# No helper copy unless asked

Do **not** invent instructional, explanatory, or “how this works” microcopy. Add helper text only when the user **explicitly asks** for that wording (or to keep copy they already specified).

## Counts as helper (do not add)

- Hints under fields (`fk-form__hint`, gray `<p>` under labels)
- Section / card subtitles that explain the feature (`semestersSectionHint`, “semesters come from settings…”)
- Footer / empty-state essays that restate the form
- Tooltips or captions that teach the workflow

## Always OK without asking

- One **field label** per control (optional marked in the label)
- **Validation / save errors** via `useFeedback()`
- **`aria-label`** on icon-only controls
- Existing copy the user did not ask to remove

```vue
<!-- BAD — unsolicited how-to -->
<h2>{{ $t('gradedCourses.semestersSection') }}</h2>
<p class="text-xs text-gray-500">{{ $t('gradedCourses.semestersSectionHint') }}</p>

<!-- GOOD — title only unless the user asked for a hint -->
<h2>{{ $t('gradedCourses.semestersSection') }}</h2>
```

If a screen already has leftover helper keys, do not add more. Remove them when the user asks, or when you are already editing that block.
